WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:05.810
The SCP Foundation has dealt with its fair
share of superheroes - from the delightful

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:14.879
SCP-2800, the prickly Scottish vigilante known
as Cactusman, to the utterly tragic SCP-2241,

00:00:14.879 --> 00:00:16.880
also known as the Superhero Wannabe.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:22.700
But we couldn’t help but wonder: What if
the SCP Foundation went up against a truly

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:27.940
evil anomalous force that simply masqueraded
as a superhero?

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:31.830
And we couldn’t think of a character who
fits this bill better than Homelander from

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:37.240
The Boys, the hit TV series produced by our
arch-nemeses at Amazon.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:42.010
Homelander is rotten to the core and has a
wide range of superpowers that allow him to

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:44.940
make his darkest desires a reality.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:49.960
And that’s why today, we’re powering up
the Anom-O-Tron 6000, filling it with all

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:56.280
three current seasons of The Boys, and posing
the big question: Could the SCP Foundation

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:01.270
bring this sadistic supe to his knees, or
is he just too diabolical?

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:03.520
Let’s find out…

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:05.640
People love superheroes.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.780
They love that warm, cozy feeling the Supes
give them.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:13.829
A golden beacon of righteousness to swoop
out of the sky and save the day, so we don’t

00:01:13.829 --> 00:01:15.270
have to do it ourselves.

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:20.389
But, you see, the thing about superheroes
is, they aren’t always nice.

00:01:20.389 --> 00:01:25.560
If the whole world holds someone up on a pedestal,
makes them believe from a young age that they

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:30.479
can do no wrong, that they’re the ultimate
paragon of virtue, and that they have the

00:01:30.479 --> 00:01:33.389
powers and freedom to do anything they want…

00:01:33.389 --> 00:01:35.639
well, you end up with him.

00:01:35.639 --> 00:01:36.639
The Homelander.

00:01:36.639 --> 00:01:41.359
Now, some look to Homelander as a hero, and
why wouldn’t they?

00:01:41.359 --> 00:01:46.270
He flies around saving people, wears those
distinctive stars and stripes on his back,

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:49.429
and stars in all those movies about how great
he is.

00:01:49.429 --> 00:01:55.219
But that’s just a cover story, the publicly
acceptable story put out by Vought, the company

00:01:55.219 --> 00:01:58.299
responsible for creating him in the first
place.

00:01:58.299 --> 00:02:02.770
They’re there to sweep under the rug any
bad thing that Homelander – or any of their

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:08.759
so-called superheroes – has ever done, so
that nobody will ever figure out the truth.

00:02:08.759 --> 00:02:09.759
And what is the truth?

00:02:09.759 --> 00:02:15.650
Well, as far as Supes go, Homelander’s even
worse than the very worst of the worst.

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:21.650
He’s a murderous, self-absorbed, narcissistic
psychopath, with no empathy for powerless

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:23.150
human beings.

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:29.140
He thinks of himself as superior to the rest
of us, ordinary people are just expendable,

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:34.790
and he’ll gladly allow an entire plane full
of innocent civilians to die with little care

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:35.840
or remorse.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:41.090
Oh, but Homelander will play all that up for
the cameras, though, which is why nobody would

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:44.080
ever think to question his status as a hero.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:49.110
As far as the public knows, Homelander’s
actions are always justified, and that he

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:54.040
can do no wrong, and it’s that mentality
that allows him to carry on doing whatever

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.270
he wants with total impunity.

00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:59.650
But what if everyone turned on Homelander?

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:05.280
Say his cover was finally blown and the rest
of the world got to see him as he really is:

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:13.030
a murderer with too much power, rampant insecurity,
an explosive temper, and some nasty lingering

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:14.030
parental issues.

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:18.740
Sure, getting a look at the real Homelander
might be a cause for celebration from his

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:24.670
most hardcore fanboys, allowing them to rally
behind what they think he stands for.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:27.730
But what if we all had enough?

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:30.599
What if everybody rejected Homelander?

00:03:30.599 --> 00:03:34.799
As it turns out, that might be the final straw
that breaks him.

00:03:34.799 --> 00:03:38.950
By his own admission, Homelander would much
prefer to be loved by everyone.

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:44.000
But, if you take that away, he’s more than
happy to settle for being feared.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:49.209
And with the level of power that he has – flight,
super strength, invulnerability, heat vision

00:03:49.209 --> 00:03:54.849
– all it would take would be a show of his
abilities in order to incite fear.

00:03:54.849 --> 00:03:56.450
And now, it’s happened.

00:03:56.450 --> 00:04:01.870
The love anyone had for Homelander is gone,
maybe his crimes have finally been exposed,

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:05.140
or he might have laser visioned someone in
broad daylight.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:10.600
Regardless of the spark that started it, the
fire has started burning, and now he’s no

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:15.389
longer chained, Homelander is free to do whatever
he wants.

00:04:15.389 --> 00:04:20.610
He started tactically, taking out key structures
of influence in the United States.

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:25.280
The White House went first, the red-hot beams
of his eye lasers carving through the entire

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:29.980
building, separating staff and secret service
members at the waist or the neck, splattering

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:31.560
the walls with blood.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:36.500
The ‘World’s Greatest Superhero’ took
care of the President personally, melting

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:39.860
him down with his heat vision before flying
away.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:44.170
Next on his list of targets was the Pentagon,
shrugging off bullets and tank shells from

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:47.970
the United States Military as they were rapidly
deployed to stop him.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:52.360
It didn’t take long for Homelander to cut
through the soldiers sent to stop him, before

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:57.010
demolishing the Pentagon with as little as
a supersonic clap of his hands.

00:04:57.010 --> 00:05:01.660
As the building crumbled around him, so did
a number of the country’s defenses fall

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:02.780
as well.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:08.760
But there was one last line of defense, one
organization that just might have access to

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:13.570
the means to bring the Only Man in the Sky
back down to group level.

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:18.500
The SCP Foundation were no strangers to powerful
beings running amok, but they were the only

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:22.170
ones with the means to oppose a rampage like
this.

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:28.040
Now, while Homelander had already decimated
much of the regular armed forces, the Foundation

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:30.580
brought an army of their own to bear.

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:35.640
Enter the Mobile Task Forces, the organization’s
most elite special operatives.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:39.741
They’re specifically trained to deal with
threats well beyond the capabilities of the

00:05:39.741 --> 00:05:45.170
regular military and can be quickly deployed
almost anywhere in the world at a moment’s

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:47.020
notice, ready for action.

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:51.820
Mobilizing their collected forces, the Foundation
dispatched its MTFs at once.

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:56.800
They had to be smart; Homelander was playing
this tactically, taking out centers of influence,

00:05:56.800 --> 00:06:01.780
and defense capabilities, still unleashing
his years’ worth of bottled-up rage but

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:05.270
using it in a controlled, calculated way.

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:09.770
If they sent every Mobile Task Force to where
Homelander was, he could easily fly away at

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:14.690
supersonic speeds, outmaneuver them – or
just disintegrate the Foundation’s entire

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:16.560
reserve of troops in one move.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:22.710
So, their primary goal was to divide and conquer,
and spread their MTFs across the country so

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:26.670
that anywhere Homelander went, they would
be waiting for him.

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:31.120
Of course, the fall of the regular military
had already shown that conventional weapons

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:33.060
had little to no effect on Homelander.

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:38.940
He is completely resistant to almost every
form of physical harm, not only completely

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:42.860
bulletproof, but unfazed by explosions as
well.

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:46.680
On top of that, his powers for detecting threats
were also unparalleled.

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:51.740
Homelander had the ability to see through
almost any solid object or surface using X-ray

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:56.470
vision; however, the Foundation knew there
was a limit to this ability, and that the

00:06:56.470 --> 00:07:00.410
Supe couldn’t see through certain metals,
specifically zinc.

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:06.770
He also has tremendous olfactory and auditory
senses, well beyond that of any ordinary human

00:07:06.770 --> 00:07:11.720
being, Homelander could detect changes in
smell on such an acute level that he could

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:17.370
detect changes to someone’s adrenaline levels,
as well as using that ability to detect explosives.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:21.950
But it was his super hearing that the Foundation
was planning to exploit.

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:27.480
They knew Homelander’s senses were so attuned
he could detect changes in a person’s heartbeat,

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.570
enough to know when someone was lying.

00:07:29.570 --> 00:07:33.450
However, having such a level of sensitive
hearing meant that Homelander had at least

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:37.490
one vulnerability: high-frequency soundwaves.

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:41.640
The Foundation knew it wouldn’t be enough
to kill the man in the sky, but they had another

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:43.790
trick up their sleeve for that.

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:49.000
First, they needed to draw him out, but how
would they when Homelander could easily overhear

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.670
the orders being broadcast to their troops?

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:53.800
Simple, they could lie.

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:58.800
The Foundation started issuing falsified directions
to its MTFs on the ground, each one followed

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:02.940
up with a written digital message via each
troop’s heads-up display.

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:07.970
All Foundation operatives were reminded to
disregard any radio communications, that these

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:13.320
weren’t real orders, merely just interference
to throw Homelander off what they were actually

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:14.320
doing.

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:17.810
While the fake radio orders were attempting
to nudge Homelander closer and closer towards

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:23.090
New York, which was where Vought Tower, his
headquarters, were located, one team was already

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:24.440
there, lying in wait.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:29.700
Mobile Task Force Pi-1, also known by the
codename ‘City Slickers’, had received

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:31.960
a coded message from the Foundation.

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:36.159
They were instructed to infiltrate Vought
Tower, retrieve an item from the company’s

00:08:36.159 --> 00:08:39.960
research and development labs, then make their
way to the roof.

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:43.330
Once they were there, the next stage of the
plan was to administer what they found in

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:48.630
R&amp;D, then await an airdrop of high-frequency
sonic weaponry that the Foundation was sending

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:49.880
to aid them.

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:53.450
Storming Vought Tower had been the surprisingly
easy part.

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:57.810
The entire company had fallen into chaos;
now that their number one product was raining

00:08:57.810 --> 00:09:02.430
death from the sky, the employees at Vought
didn’t seem to care much about their jobs

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:03.430
anymore.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:08.430
The City Slickers had snuck into the laboratory
and found what they were sent for: Temporary

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:14.191
Compound V, a chemical that would alter human
biology and grant anyone superpowers for a

00:09:14.191 --> 00:09:15.740
twenty-four-hour period.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:20.150
It had the nasty side effect of turning the
user’s brain into Swiss cheese, but under

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:23.630
the circumstances, it seemed necessary.

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:28.610
Dosing themselves with it, all of the Slickers
were in agony as they felt the V24 burning

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:29.930
in their veins.

00:09:29.930 --> 00:09:34.540
Just as the chopper was arriving to drop off
their weaponry, a loud, booming sound rang

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:39.340
out, shattering windows across the city as
Homelander’s approach broke the sound barrier.

00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:44.130
The MTF stared up in horror as his laser vision
cut through the helicopter above their heads,

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:48.450
one of the crates landing on the roof as the
fiery wreck plummeted down towards the street.

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:49.450
“Jackson!”

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:51.730
the team leader yelled to one of his men,
before pausing.

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:57.080
He knew if he told him to retrieve the sonic
cannon, Homelander would destroy it in seconds.

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:01.300
Instead, Jackson watched as his commanding
officer leaped up into the air, hundreds of

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:04.400
feet higher than he would normally have been
capable of.

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:09.560
He careened towards a surprised Homelander,
swinging a Compound V-fuelled uppercut that

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:14.080
connected with his jaw, reeling him slightly
as he hovered above.

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:17.630
Taking that as their cue, the other members
of the City Slickers started attacking the

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:19.380
out-of-control Supe.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:23.700
One of them was firing energy blasts from
his palms, and another had her arms stretching

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:27.840
out like rubber, grabbing the Homelander’s
cape in an attempt to drag him out of the

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:28.840
sky.

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:33.420
Meanwhile, Jackson was scrabbling across the
roof of the Tower, fumbling with the clasps

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.900
on the crate that contained the weapon.

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:41.130
He could hear snarling behind him, as Homelander
roared in disapproval, disgusted that these

00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:44.529
so-called ‘ordinary people’ were daring
to attack him.

00:10:44.529 --> 00:10:49.450
His heat vision burned through the City Slicker’s
uniforms, but couldn’t pierce their skin.

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:53.580
Enraged, Homelander gripped the commander’s
head as he made another jump towards, him,

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:57.150
pushing both his super-strong hands together
until he could hear the man’s skull beginning

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:59.910
to crack… then he kept squeezing.

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:04.270
Flattening the commander between his palms,
Homelander flew downwards, landing a dual-fisted

00:11:04.270 --> 00:11:07.780
punch that burst through the chests of the
other two Slickers.

00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:13.370
He pulled both hands back, his red gloves,
like the rest of his uniform, already slickened

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:15.520
with copious amounts of blood.

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:22.400
Then, a loud, shrieking sound pierced his
attuned ears as Jackson fired the sonic cannon.

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:26.480
The cacophony of high-frequency soundwaves
it emitted were deafening to Homelander’s

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:30.800
attuned, sensitive ears, sending pain shooting
through his head.

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:36.279
Unfortunately, pain meant little to Homelander,
and he could still function despite it.

00:11:36.279 --> 00:11:40.740
It angered him even further that someone was
trying to best him, that they’d highlighted

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:46.220
and tried to exploit a weakness – something
the Supe had told himself he didn’t have.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:51.040
He shot forwards lightning-fast, wrenching
the device out of Jackson’s hands before

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:56.150
gripping him by the throat, lifting him up
off his feet so he was dangling over the edge

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:57.150
of the tower.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:12:00.660
“Who in the hell do you think you are?”

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:06.130
Homelander muttered, disturbingly subdued
despite the obvious, unhinged look in his

00:12:06.130 --> 00:12:07.130
eyes.

00:12:07.130 --> 00:12:08.130
“Just…”

00:12:08.130 --> 00:12:11.790
Jackson gasped for breath as he felt fingers
clasping around his fault; in the distance

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:14.779
there was a low, rhythmic rumbling, like an
earthquake…

00:12:14.779 --> 00:12:16.620
or heavy footsteps getting closer.

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:18.560
“Just a distraction.”

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:23.020
With that, Homelander’s hand closed tight,
the very second that Jackson teleported out

00:12:23.020 --> 00:12:27.560
of his grip, leaving the Supe standing on
the roof alone, save for the bodies of the

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:28.680
other City Slickers.

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:33.339
He turned to face the sound of the oncoming
footsteps, detecting the sound of whirring

00:12:33.339 --> 00:12:35.470
machinery along with it.

00:12:35.470 --> 00:12:36.940
This was something new.

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:41.070
It was rare for Homelander to ever face a
real challenge.

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:43.970
Nothing ever forced him to improve his skills
in combat.

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:48.930
In most cases, he could just rely on his strength,
or bring a quick end to confrontations with

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:55.700
his eye lasers, which made the sight of SCP-5514
approaching all the more surprising to him.

00:12:55.700 --> 00:13:01.020
Striding across the city like something out
of a Pacific Rim movie was a gigantic mech,

00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:08.070
known as SCP-5514 or by its far cooler sounding
nickname The Dragonslayer.

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:13.110
Working with the Global Occult Coalition and
Hy-Brasil, the Foundation themselves constructed

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:19.630
SCP-5514, using various anomalous methods,
designing the machine to combat Large Scale

00:13:19.630 --> 00:13:21.779
Aggressors, or LSAs.

00:13:21.779 --> 00:13:26.690
While the Dragonslayer – like the name implies
– was built with fighting monsters and kaiju

00:13:26.690 --> 00:13:32.520
similar to its own size, these desperate times
had called for desperate measures.

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:38.350
The mech’s huge, robotic arm hoisted its
primary weapon, a Cold Iron Sword; its blade

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:39.760
twenty meters long.

00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:45.740
Inside, members of Mobile Task Force Eta-5,
the Jäeger Bombers, were piloting the Dragonslayer,

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:47.370
readying for battle with Homelander.

00:13:47.370 --> 00:13:52.550
He was staying still, not attempting to run
or even fly away, instead, he stayed at the

00:13:52.550 --> 00:13:53.690
top of Vought Tower.

00:13:53.690 --> 00:14:00.140
It was like he was waiting, watching, unfazed
by the approaching humanoid machine, looking

00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:03.250
right at it... or through it.

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:07.720
The Dragonslayer brought its Cold Iron Sword
swooping down through the air, the blade coming

00:14:07.720 --> 00:14:10.120
right down on where Homelander stood.

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:15.680
It cleaved directly through the building beneath
him, carving Vought Tower in two, sending

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:19.200
a shower of glass and concrete over the plaza
below.

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:24.450
The Supe caught the blade as it came at him,
screaming in pain as he felt it cut into his

00:14:24.450 --> 00:14:25.450
hands.

00:14:25.450 --> 00:14:30.540
Any wound left by the Cold Iron Sword was
permanent, there was no regenerating or recovering

00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:31.540
from it.

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:35.960
Homelander’s natural durability gave him
an edge, that and being so much smaller than

00:14:35.960 --> 00:14:39.570
the sword itself, allowed him not to be sliced
to pieces.

00:14:39.570 --> 00:14:41.670
But even touching it through his gloves hurt.

00:14:41.670 --> 00:14:46.920
The Tower was rubble, Homelander was down,
but far from out.

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:51.550
He climbed up through the debris and bodies
he was buried under, not caring when he blasted

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:55.240
his heat vision through the dead and wounded
to clear a path back up.

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:58.680
Looming above, the Dragonslayer stood taller
than most buildings.

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:04.040
His eyes glowing both with anger and the red
light of his lasers, Homelander pushed himself

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:06.960
up off the ground and flew up into the air.

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:11.029
The mech’s arm moved weightlessly to swat
him out of the air, but Homelander used his

00:15:11.029 --> 00:15:15.810
speed and momentum to shoot through the metal,
ripping through the machine’s hand before

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:17.570
it could land a strike.

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:21.250
Homelander started zipping out of the path
of the Dragonslayer as it opened fire with

00:15:21.250 --> 00:15:23.050
its various anomalous armaments.

00:15:23.050 --> 00:15:29.040
While the mech was primarily used for close-quarters
melee combat with various LSAs, it also featured

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:31.420
a number of longer-range weaponry.

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:37.940
Mounted on SCP-551’s shoulder was a Beowulf-Sigurd
Railgun, an anomalous weapon that could use

00:15:37.940 --> 00:15:42.470
altered gravity to affect the weight of its
targets, causing projectiles to impact with

00:15:42.470 --> 00:15:43.550
higher velocity.

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:48.700
Yet, none of these projectiles landed a shot,
unable to catch Homelander at his current

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:49.850
flight speed.

00:15:49.850 --> 00:15:53.980
With every supersonic pass he made of the
Dragonslayer, the deranged Supe took another

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:55.850
look at his current enemy.

00:15:55.850 --> 00:16:00.280
His X-ray eyes could penetrate most of the
metal and gave him a clear enough view of

00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:01.370
what was inside.

00:16:01.370 --> 00:16:08.490
There was a miniature sun powering it, kept
perpetually stable while it generated energy

00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:09.830
for SCP-5514.

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:13.990
Surrounding it were sub-dimensional portals,
venting the excess heat off this plane of

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:16.870
reality so that the mech and nothing around
it melted.

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:22.459
A similar process was moving some of the substantial
weight of the mech into a tiny pocket dimension,

00:16:22.459 --> 00:16:26.680
which had allowed it to move so swiftly without
being too cumbersome.

00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:30.000
Piloting it were humans, more MTF operatives.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:34.800
Spotting them through the metal hull, Homelander
flew towards the Dragonslayer like a bullet.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:38.810
The force of the impact caused the mech to
wobble slightly as Homelander shot through

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:40.640
the outer layers of armor.

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:46.029
He came bursting out into the main chamber,
eyes burning intense lasers through the vital

00:16:46.029 --> 00:16:47.950
inner components of the Dragonslayer.

00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:53.880
The beams sliced the unprotected MTFs up,
reducing them to a bloody paste before Homelander

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:56.970
turned his rage towards the power source.

00:16:56.970 --> 00:17:00.700
Ripping through more of the metalwork, he
looked at the housing for the sub-dimensional

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:03.510
portals venting out the mini sun’s heat.

00:17:03.510 --> 00:17:08.020
Though he had a limited understanding of what
exactly this all was, Homelander could make

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:10.059
sense of what it was doing.

00:17:10.059 --> 00:17:14.049
He fired off another series of blasts with
his heat beams, tearing through the devices

00:17:14.049 --> 00:17:19.419
that regulated the portals, before flying
back out of the Dragonslayer as fast as he

00:17:19.419 --> 00:17:20.419
could.

00:17:20.419 --> 00:17:24.179
Landing at its feet, he looked up to see his
despicable handiwork.

00:17:24.179 --> 00:17:30.049
From within, the sub-dimensional portals began
pulling the insides of SCP-5514 in different

00:17:30.049 --> 00:17:35.499
directions, pulling it apart and sucking it
into different pocket dimensions as it collapsed

00:17:35.499 --> 00:17:37.299
in on itself.

00:17:37.299 --> 00:17:42.820
Homelander sighed, the tiniest hint of fatigue
he felt passing in a fleeting moment, gone

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:45.539
before the Dragonslayer eventually fell.

00:17:45.539 --> 00:17:47.299
“Enough, cease this villainy!”

00:17:47.299 --> 00:17:49.610
a voice called from nearby.

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:54.809
Homelander sighed in exasperation to face
this latest nuisance that dared oppose him.

00:17:54.809 --> 00:17:59.320
When he saw the shadowy figure approaching
him, he was taken aback at first, thinking

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:01.799
he recognised who it was.

00:18:01.799 --> 00:18:04.279
“Noir?” he asked in disbelief.

00:18:04.279 --> 00:18:08.870
“No, that is not my name,” the dark-clad
figure announced.

00:18:08.870 --> 00:18:12.059
“Homelander of the Seven, your time has
come!

00:18:12.059 --> 00:18:15.159
For now, you face The Specter!”

00:18:15.159 --> 00:18:20.980
The Specter, otherwise known as SCP-4494,
was the physical embodiment of crime fighting

00:18:20.980 --> 00:18:21.980
itself.

00:18:21.980 --> 00:18:27.039
Its long, dark cloak whipped in the wind,
a wide-brimmed hat pulled low, giving it the

00:18:27.039 --> 00:18:29.700
appearance of a shadowy gunslinger.

00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:34.919
From head to toe, The Specter seemed to pull
all light on the visible spectrum into itself,

00:18:34.919 --> 00:18:37.870
making it look like a ghostly shadow come
to life.

00:18:37.870 --> 00:18:41.790
“And how the hell do they expect you to
stop me?”

00:18:41.790 --> 00:18:42.850
Homelander sneered.

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:49.190
“I go wherever injustice reigns,” The
Specter replied, not short on dramatic flair.

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:53.990
“And you have unleashed horrific, unspeakable
terror on the innocents of this world.

00:18:53.990 --> 00:18:58.259
I will ask you once, and once only: stop this.

00:18:58.259 --> 00:18:59.460
Walk away.”

00:18:59.460 --> 00:19:02.080
Immediately, Homelander started laughing.

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:03.080
“Really?

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:06.960
That’s all you’ve got?” he scoffed.

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:08.239
“Just asking nicely?”

00:19:08.239 --> 00:19:12.130
“You have lost your way,” SCP-4494 declared.

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:14.840
“All this destruction, and for what?

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:16.370
Just to display your power?

00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:19.119
To subjugate, make people fear you?

00:19:19.119 --> 00:19:23.299
Or are you still trying to win the approval
of a mother and father you never had?”

00:19:23.299 --> 00:19:28.019
That last sentence struck a nerve with Homelander,
enough to make him zip forward, launching

00:19:28.019 --> 00:19:29.970
a punch at The Specter.

00:19:29.970 --> 00:19:36.460
His fist passed through a dark fog that took
the place of its intended target, as SCP-4494

00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:38.779
dissipated and then reformed behind Homelander.

00:19:38.779 --> 00:19:43.649
It put two shadowy arms around his neck, gripping
the maddened Supe in a headlock.

00:19:43.649 --> 00:19:46.909
“You were made to be a hero,” The Specter
whispered.

00:19:46.909 --> 00:19:49.450
“Look at how far you’ve fallen.”

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:54.240
Homelander angrily wrenched the arm away and
threw his captor over his head, only for the

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:59.190
Spectre to become mist again, surrounding
the hero in a thick, black cloud.

00:19:59.190 --> 00:20:03.789
He fired his heat vision again, the beams
passing through the layer of fog without causing

00:20:03.789 --> 00:20:04.789
any damage.

00:20:04.789 --> 00:20:09.659
“It’s over, Homelander, no longer will
you terrorize the innocent,” came a booming,

00:20:09.659 --> 00:20:11.190
dramatic voice from all angles.

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:15.970
“You are not the hero you think of yourself
as, but a villain.

00:20:15.970 --> 00:20:18.480
This mistake stops here!”

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:20.120
“This isn’t a mistake.

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:21.950
I don't make mistakes!”

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:22.950
Homelander roared.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:25.899
“I’m not like the rest of you, I’m stronger,
smarter.

00:20:25.899 --> 00:20:26.899
I’m better.

00:20:26.899 --> 00:20:27.899
I am better.

00:20:27.899 --> 00:20:29.230
I’m the real hero!”

00:20:29.230 --> 00:20:30.470
“Are you?”

00:20:30.470 --> 00:20:32.789
echoed The Specter’s voice.

00:20:32.789 --> 00:20:38.090
Something thin and papery landed at Homelander’s
feet, the fog dissipating again as the Spectre

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:39.620
stood before him.

00:20:39.620 --> 00:20:44.570
Confused, Homelander picked up the papery
object, it was a comic book, the words ‘Action

00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:46.590
Comics’ emblazoned on the top.

00:20:46.590 --> 00:20:51.619
The cover showed a man dressed much like himself,
lifting an old green car above his head, his

00:20:51.619 --> 00:20:56.049
red cape billowing in the win, a letter ‘S’
worn across his chest.

00:20:56.049 --> 00:20:58.970
As he flicked through the pages, tears formed
in Homelander’s eyes.

00:20:58.970 --> 00:21:02.870
“This is what you think you are,” The
Specter said solemnly.

00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:07.090
“But look around, look at the lives you’ve
taken or ruined.

00:21:07.090 --> 00:21:08.409
A hero?

00:21:08.409 --> 00:21:11.109
No, heroism is not subjugating others.

00:21:11.109 --> 00:21:13.830
Not viewing yourself as superior.

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:18.379
Heroism is realizing we are all the same,
and standing up to those that would try to

00:21:18.379 --> 00:21:19.519
disagree.”

00:21:19.519 --> 00:21:22.720
The Spectre brought his dark cloak around
Homelander’s shoulder.

00:21:22.720 --> 00:21:29.480
There were no survivors around to see where
they went or to hear SCP-4494’s final words.

00:21:29.480 --> 00:21:32.409
“You aren’t a real hero.”

00:21:32.409 --> 00:21:34.019
And then they were gone…

00:21:34.019 --> 00:21:38.749
Now, if you want to see another clash between
a comic book legend and one of the most infamously

00:21:38.749 --> 00:21:44.859
dangerous anomalies, go and check out “DEADPOOL
VS SCP-682” to see the Merc with the Mouth

00:21:44.859 --> 00:21:47.260
battling the Hard to Destroy Reptile.

00:21:47.260 --> 00:21:51.759
Then after that, if you’re in the mood for
another chaotic match-up, witness the galaxy’s

00:21:51.759 --> 00:21:56.729
greatest bounty hunter taking on the Flesh
that Hates in “BOBA FETT VS SCP-610”!

